    "problemStatement": "For an array BBB of MMM **distinct** positive integers, we define a function F(B)F(B)F(B) as follows:\n\n\nInitialise an empty array CCC and mark all indices of BBB (from 111 to MMM) as unmarked.\nRepeat the following step exactly MMM times:\n\nChoose an unmarked index iii that is adjacent to a marked index (or any index in the first iteration).\nAppend BiB_iBi​ to the end of CCC.\nMark index iii.\n\n\nF(B)F(B)F(B) is defined as the lexicographically smallest†^\\dag† array CCC that can be obtained through this process.\nStack has a permutation‡^\\ddag‡ PPP of length NNN.\n\nLet Qi=F(P[1,i])Q_i = F(P[1,i])Qi​=F(P[1,i]). He wants you to construct an array AAA of length NNN such that:\n\n\nFor each 1≤i≤N1\\le i\\le N1≤i≤N, QAiQ_{A_i}QAi​​ is the ithi^{th}ith lexicographically smallest array among the set of arrays Qi&nbsp;(1≤i≤N)Q_i \\ (1\\le i \\le N)Qi​&nbsp;(1≤i≤N) .\n†^\\dag†An array XXX is lexicographically smaller than an array YYY if one of the following holds:\n\n\nXXX is a prefix of YYY and X≠YX \\ne YX=Y;\nIn the first position where XXX and YYY differ, Xi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​.\n‡^\\ddag‡A permutation of length NNN consists of all integers from 111 to NNN exactly once. P[1,j]P[1,j]P[1,j] denotes the subarray [P1,P2,…,Pj][P_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_j][P1​,P2​,…,Pj​] of permutation PPP.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the permutation PPP.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1,P_2,\\ldots,P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​ representing the permutation PPP.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print NNN space-separated integers, A1,A2,…ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots A_NA1​,A2​,…AN​, denoting the array AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Pi≤N1 \\leq P_i \\leq N1≤Pi​≤N",
      "All elements of PPP are distinct.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
